From 9d5e18537c7480f0e2fee9c63ff0e957ba3d44a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mrsirg97-rgb <mrsirg97@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:34:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] DeepSeek: keep conversations aside, so an agent's parent
 and workers don't re-read each other's prompts

MAYA_DS4_SLOT_KEEP=1 sets a conversation aside when another one takes the model - its whole state, the
compressed KV and index keys included - and a request that continues it reads only its new tokens; the
conversations outlive the engine in MAYA_DS4_SLOT_DIR, capped by MAYA_DS4_SLOT_CAP (RAM) and MAYA_DS4_SLOT_GB
(the folder). Off by default. A fresh engine holds 0 tokens, which no prompt continues, so a restart's first
request takes the folder's slot instead of reading from token 0.

tools/ds4/slot_keep_test.py: A, B, A's next turn in one run (reused = A's full prefix), the same from the
folder after a restart, greedy tokens against a no-keep reference (real text, the turn built from the
reference's answer so the prompts are identical), and a third conversation forcing the LRU out of the folder.

(cherry picked from commit 993b566a024b15394c411c3db9a4c91589fbb92c)
(cherry picked from commit 08ad5852c65fc8c374d7d1405948b3fd7147404d)
